%N A000758 Sum over rooted plane trees with n edges of (height - 1); height = measured edges.
%C A000758 From _Siddhartha Mahajan_, Aug 23 2026: (Start)
%C A000758 Equivalently, a(n) counts pairs (T,k), where T is a rooted plane tree with n edges and 2 <= k <= height(T). Hence a(n) = A136439(n) - A000108(n).
%C A000758 Frederic Cazals could not recover the original definition or code when contacted by Sean A. Irvine. The new definition reproduces all 10 original terms, but it is not known whether this was exactly the statistic intended by Cazals. (End)
%D A000758 Frederic Cazals, Path lengths in plane trees, preprint
%H A000758 Siddhartha Mahajan, <a href="/A000758/b000758.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A000758 Siddhartha Mahajan, <a href="https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/seqfan/824b7202-e208-4d74-b1bf-52ec3ec83e06n%40googlegroups.com">SeqFan discussion: A000758, possible identification and relation to A136439</a> (2026).
%H A000758 <a href="/index/Ro#rooted">Index entries for sequences related to rooted trees</a>
%F A000758 From _Siddhartha Mahajan_, Aug 23 2026: (Start)
%F A000758 a(n) = A136439(n) - A000108(n).
%F A000758 a(n) = A261003(n) - 2*A000108(n).
%F A000758 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} (k-1)*A080936(n,k). (End)
%Y A000758 Cf. A000108, A080936, A136439, A261003.
%K A000758 nonn,changed
%O A000758 1,3
